---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="LS Academy | Franco Lopez" description="LS Academy is a Moodle learning platform on Kubernetes for 500+ LS Tractor dealers, employees, and U.S. LS Group affiliates.">
  <header class="page-header">
    <span class="eyebrow">learning platform · kubernetes</span>
    <h1>LS Academy</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      A Moodle learning platform on Kubernetes for LS Tractor dealers, employees, and U.S. LS Group
      affiliates.
    </p>
  </header>

  <article class="content">
    <h2>Problem</h2>
    <p>
      Dealer training needed a platform that could scale beyond one-off documents and manual delivery,
      and that made training easier to publish, access, maintain, and measure.
    </p>

    <h2>What I built</h2>
    <p>
      I developed and support LS Academy, a Moodle learning management system (LMS) used by 500+
      dealers, employees, and U.S. LS Group affiliates for training and onboarding. It runs on
      Kubernetes and is deployed through Argo CD and GitHub Actions, so every change goes through Git.
    </p>

    <h2>Operational focus</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Simple deployment and rollback paths</li>
      <li>Clear ownership of the application, data, and infrastructure layers</li>
      <li>User access and administrative workflows</li>
      <li>Documentation that keeps the platform easy to operate</li>
    </ul>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
